10	 * showed corruption concentrated on the FIRST indices of the inner loop
11	 * (idx 0 + idx 1 = 36/55 records) while the buffer spans 1024 entries.
12	 * This variant walks the 1024 vector slots in a REVISED order — even
13	 * outer iterations sweep ascending, odd outer iterations descending — so
14	 * the touch pattern at idx 0/1 differs (on a descending pass, index 0 is
15	 * the LAST slot touched, with a fully-warm pipeline behind it, and the
16	 * store->load adjacency across the loop seam changes).
17	 *   strong idx-0/1 signal also here -> the signature follows the buffer
18	 *      slots themselves (address-local, e.g. same L1D set/way)
19	 *   signature moves to the sweep seam / disappears ->
20	 *      it follows the forward-progress position in the sweep
21	 * Same skeleton as the parent otherwise: 3rd ldr (scratch, discarded) at
22	 * top + 2-source ldr z loads + rotating svadd/sveor/svand/svorr per slot
23	 * (slot%4) + back-to-back str temp / str dst; memcmp in the cold path.
24	 * @endparblock
25	 */
